t the value of `usable_content` to include both parts clearly.\n\n    *   Wait, one more thing: \"Different settings... start by stating inconsistency\".\n    *   Inconsistency: Human trial data reports immune/metabolic shifts, whereas causal mediation of clinical efficacy is supported by mouse models; direct statistical mediation in humans is not explicitly quantified in the provided comparisons.\n    *   Then details.\n\n    *   Let's draft the text.\n    *   \"Inconsistency: Human DIET trial data reports immune profiling and metabolomic changes, while causal mediation of ICI efficacy is demonstrated in mouse avatar models; direct statistical mediation linking human microbiome changes to clinical outcomes (ORR/PFS/OS) is not explicitly reported in the provided comparisons.\n    *   Positive Findings: High fiber arm vs control arm showed significant decreases in circulating macrophages (p=.018) and neutrophils (p=.035) by NanoString, and classical monocytes (p=.0059) by CyTOF at Week 5-8. CyTOF showed increased CD8+ (p=.01) and CD4+ effector-memory T cells (p=.032) in high fiber arm. Bile acid metabolism changed significantly (p<0.05). Mouse recipients of post-high fiber microbiota showed improved ICB response.\n    *   Non-Significant Trends: Classical monocytes (NanoString) and dendritic cells (p=.06 each) did not reach significance.\n    *   Subgroup: Findings more prominent in combination nivolumab + ipilimumab (n=3) vs monotherapy (n=7).\n    *   Limitation: Specific statistical mediation analysis of human microbiome taxa/function to clinical efficacy is not detailed in provided statistics.\n    *   Applicable Conditions: DIET trial (NCT04645680) early abstracts (6743, 3275, LB109); distinguishes between human observational immune/metabolic data and mouse causal data.\"\n\n    *   Refining for compactness and constraints.\n    *   Ensure I don't say \"fiber caused\". Say \"high fiber arm showed...\".\n    *   Ensure I don't claim human mediation exists.\n    *